# The [[condition#Noun|condition]] of a [[system]] in which [[competing#Adjective|competing]] [[influence#Noun|influences]] are [[balance#Verb|balanced]], resulting in no [[net#Noun|net]] [[change#Noun|change]].
#* {{RQ:Miller Gardeners Dictionary|volume=I|entry=HYDROSTATICKS|page=341|column=1|passage=To ''Hydroſtaticks'' belong whatever relates to the Gravities and '''Equilibria''' of Liquors; with the Art of weighing Bodies in Water, in order to eſtimate the ſpecifick Gravities.}}
#* '''1999''', ''[[w:The Matrix|The Matrix]]'', Agent Smith speech
#*: Every mammal on this planet instinctively develops a natural '''equilibrium''' with the surrounding environment but you humans do not. You move to an area and you multiply and multiply until every natural resource is consumed and the only way you can survive is to spread to another area. There is another organism on this planet that follows the same pattern. Do you know what it is? A virus.
#: {{syn|en|balance|stability}}
#: {{ant|en|disequilibrium|imbalance|instability}}
# [[mental|Mental]] [[balance#Noun|balance]].
#: {{syn|en|sanity}}
#: {{ant|en|insanity|instability|madness}}
#* {{quote-av|en|title=w:The Eric Andre Show|year=2020|season=5|number=6|passage={{w|Tiffany Pollard|Tiffany Pollard}}: What just happened?!<br/>{{w|Eric Andre|Eric Andre}}: That coffee mug is broken.<br/>Tiffany Pollard: I can't take this. This is gonna mess up my '''equilibrium'''.}}
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} The [[state#Noun|state]] of a [[reaction]] in which the [[rate#Noun|rates]] of the [[forward]] and [[reverse]] reactions are the same.
# {{lb|en|physics}} The state of a [[body]] at [[rest#Noun|rest]] or in [[uniform#Adjective|uniform]] [[motion]] in which the [[resultant#Noun|resultant]] of all [[force#Noun|forces]] on it is [[zero]].
